                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "48fd483e-16a1-3575-aef2-ef465c7c5b41",
                        "entry_id": "e7ef418a-aec9-3836-b711-9778888cb3be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. владение рабами, использование рабов, рабства; также общественный строй, при котором существует рабство"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea0ede20-0603-4b49-9b4b-ae9b0725e530",
                                "sense_id": "48fd483e-16a1-3575-aef2-ef465c7c5b41",
                                "text": "Припомним, что землевладельческие понятия и привычки древней Руси выработались на рабовладении; древние землевладельцы эксплуатировали свои вотчины преимущественно при помощи рабов."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7fc97d56-797b-46a2-801c-3f14c470d7d2",
                                "sense_id": "48fd483e-16a1-3575-aef2-ef465c7c5b41",
                                "text": "Так привычно жить народу (к счастью, не всему!) в полуинтернатских условиях всего бесплатного, не задумываясь о том, как каждую секунду буквально съедалось богатейшее государство, а видимость прогресса обеспечивало рабовладение ГУЛАГа."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f90abcc1-892a-4548-8590-dbadc4e4813f",
                        "source_entry_id": "e7ef418a-aec9-3836-b711-9778888cb3be",
                        "source_sense_id": "48fd483e-16a1-3575-aef2-ef465c7c5b41",
                        "target_lang_word": "slaveholding",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "slaveholding",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e61e6758-d830-32bd-b2a8-2484912ccd50",
                                        "entry_id": "20bf1b92-4259-379e-86fb-99938d7542dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having possession/ownership of one or more slaves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "slaveholding",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eff2d94f-b3c9-335a-89bf-e8b84b57497b",
                                        "entry_id": "080f4eff-7d62-3fde-9c8b-fba19e66c554",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The institution or practice of owning slaves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2cadf75e-9287-4959-a4f6-8072cb01048e",
                                                "sense_id": "eff2d94f-b3c9-335a-89bf-e8b84b57497b",
                                                "text": "The slaveholding way of life continued until 1865, when the Thirteenth Amendment to the U.S. Constitution was passed following the end of the Civil War between the Northern and the Southern states"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1acfff2-231f-42f7-8e4b-a3edc78bacf7",
                                                "sense_id": "eff2d94f-b3c9-335a-89bf-e8b84b57497b",
                                                "text": "Defenders of Southern slavery employed religious rhetoric to justify the system, selecting biblical passages that appeared to condone the practice of slaveholding and the relation between master and slave."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2581fc56-ed0c-3e92-a3b1-dbb25981d019",
                                        "entry_id": "080f4eff-7d62-3fde-9c8b-fba19e66c554",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An owning of one or more slaves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a67514c-04a3-4696-8008-a40944274fef",
                                                "sense_id": "2581fc56-ed0c-3e92-a3b1-dbb25981d019",
                                                "text": "On the other hand, the Mountain South also contained some Lower South counties, thereby permitting internal comparisons between differently sized slaveholdings, between crop specializations, and between agricultural and nonagricultural producers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2449a727-873b-4fe0-8a59-fc330a505aff",
                        "source_entry_id": "e7ef418a-aec9-3836-b711-9778888cb3be",
                        "source_sense_id": "48fd483e-16a1-3575-aef2-ef465c7c5b41",
                        "target_lang_word": "slave-owning",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c135b846-4611-4bd2-ad47-796b0d51c43a",
                        "source_entry_id": "e7ef418a-aec9-3836-b711-9778888cb3be",
                        "source_sense_id": "48fd483e-16a1-3575-aef2-ef465c7c5b41",
                        "target_lang_word": "slavery",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "slavery",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2365c801-713c-3b14-9324-1f9f5f2f749f",
                                        "entry_id": "441ec83e-510c-3430-a261-63e1a46f48e8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An institution or social practice of owning human beings as property, especially for use as forced laborers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd1e8ba3-7f85-4ffc-80b0-a7a366c2658a",
                                                "sense_id": "2365c801-713c-3b14-9324-1f9f5f2f749f",
                                                "text": "Slavery was abolished in the nineteenth century."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60acddc7-49f3-44d5-8995-e67692afec70",
                                                "sense_id": "2365c801-713c-3b14-9324-1f9f5f2f749f",
                                                "text": "The film portrays the brutality of slavery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55f53cbb-d103-44d0-b437-d2d496b089e6",
                                                "sense_id": "2365c801-713c-3b14-9324-1f9f5f2f749f",
                                                "text": "modern slavery"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8842a893-e26f-4919-8fe9-678169269371",
                                                "sense_id": "2365c801-713c-3b14-9324-1f9f5f2f749f",
                                                "text": "slavery system"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4307b2fd-ca26-46ff-9aa2-7883b42f59c6",
                                                "sense_id": "2365c801-713c-3b14-9324-1f9f5f2f749f",
                                                "text": "abolition of slavery"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5e7d491-8998-482f-9dfe-170e99deb839",
                                                "sense_id": "2365c801-713c-3b14-9324-1f9f5f2f749f",
                                                "text": "THAT the Constitution does not confer upon Congress power to interfere with slavery in the States, has been admitted by all parties and confirmed by all judicial decisions ever since the origin of the Federal Government. This doctrine was emphatically recognized by the House of Representatives in the days of Washington, during the first session of the first Congress,* and has never since been seriously called in question. Hence, it became necessary for the abolitionists, in order to furnish a pretext for their assaults on Southern slavery, to appeal to a law higher than the Constitution.\nSlavery, according to them, was a grievous sin against God, and therefore no human Constitution could rightfully shield it from destruction. It was sinful to live in a political confederacy which tolerated slavery in any of the States composing it;[...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ae74d15-bf66-41c3-969c-daf712bc0766",
                                                "sense_id": "2365c801-713c-3b14-9324-1f9f5f2f749f",
                                                "text": "Thus Django becomes the carrier of the “public use of one's reason”—the Kantian road to enlightenment given to him by the German “Forty-Eighter” dentist–turned-bounty hunter Dr. “King” Schultz, and represents the fictive, allohistorical beginning of the battle against slavery and racism in the United States."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a0d69749-e534-3831-8e09-7ef21ead5859",
                                        "entry_id": "441ec83e-510c-3430-a261-63e1a46f48e8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Forced labor in general, regardless of legality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6d62461-e239-3df9-a5c3-81c5174d4123",
                                        "entry_id": "441ec83e-510c-3430-a261-63e1a46f48e8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A condition of servitude endured by a slave."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92abb467-ebe3-4456-b566-a5d96eb2cc5e",
                                                "sense_id": "e6d62461-e239-3df9-a5c3-81c5174d4123",
                                                "text": "If you wil willingly remaine with me,\nYou ſhall haue honors, as your merits be:\nOr els you ſhal be forc’d with ſlauerie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6abe62a3-ab78-4234-96a8-adbac2247606",
                                                "sense_id": "e6d62461-e239-3df9-a5c3-81c5174d4123",
                                                "text": "Our victories on Voeld are only the beginning of what we can achieve, but we can't defeat the enemy without your help. If you're tired of living in fear, if you believe we were meant for something greater than slavery, if you're willing to stand up and fight: you'll find a new family in the Resistance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "42a874cf-aeda-3643-9dd0-3c291b86a496",
                                        "entry_id": "441ec83e-510c-3430-a261-63e1a46f48e8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A condition in which one is captivated or subjugated, as by greed or drugs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8f03787-a5ad-489b-86d4-040f27e47d5f",
                                                "sense_id": "42a874cf-aeda-3643-9dd0-3c291b86a496",
                                                "text": "Man seeks for gold in mines that he may weave / A lasting chain for his own slavery."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "slavery",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f744d0f-30ce-35c0-9a03-d44594773a7e",
                                        "entry_id": "e0a25fa2-5751-397e-8fbc-a40087097b5f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Covered in slaver; slobbery."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9cb7dcea-e592-4aaf-b22d-7f620879e534",
                                                "sense_id": "4f744d0f-30ce-35c0-9a03-d44594773a7e",
                                                "text": "The giant snow bear, the wolf with slavery jaws or the claws of the silent great cats were all a part. Creatures of man's oldest nightmares were the other side of that face."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
